From 6071010c303d0c8d4416c43cdee20a0f2e769d37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raul Moran <rmg@raulmoranguerra.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:37:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tests: nucleo_wba52cg: Expect the input capture of an ARR + 1
 period

TIM_PWMInput measures a PWM signal whose period is ARR + 1 timer clocks
on the chip. STM32_Timer now counts ARR + 1 values per period, so the
captured period (IC2) is 50000 and 33333 instead of 49999 and 33332, and
the second duty cycle (IC1 * 100 / IC2 in integers) 49 % instead of 50 %.
---
 tests/platforms/nucleo_wba52cg.robot | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/platforms/nucleo_wba52cg.robot b/tests/platforms/nucleo_wba52cg.robot
index 872cef3..e825ac2 100644
--- a/tests/platforms/nucleo_wba52cg.robot
+++ b/tests/platforms/nucleo_wba52cg.robot
@@ -60,9 +60,9 @@ Timer Should Support Input Capture
 
     Check Input Capture Line        frequency=0     duty=0   IC2=0
     Execute Command                 sysbus.gpioPortC.UserButton1 PressAndRelease
-    Check Input Capture Line        frequency=2000  duty=24  IC2=49999
+    Check Input Capture Line        frequency=2000  duty=24  IC2=50000
     Execute Command                 sysbus.gpioPortC.UserButton1 PressAndRelease
-    Check Input Capture Line        frequency=3000  duty=50  IC2=33332
+    Check Input Capture Line        frequency=3000  duty=49  IC2=33333
 
 Should Have Working UART
     Create Machine                  ${UART_PRINTF}
-- 
2.51.0

